hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1312","Narrated by Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Jawhari, narrated by Marwan bin Muawiyah, Ibn Numayr, and Ya’la, on the authority of Abu Suqa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, h. Al-Jawhari also narrated to us Hussein bin Muhammad Abu Ahmad, on the authority of Asim bin Omar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, and those did not dismiss it as: “Whoever sniffles in the direction of the qiblah of the mosque will be resurrected while it is in his face.”"
"1313","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, Shababah told us, Asim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who phlegms will be raised to face the Qiblah on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be in his face.”"
"1314","Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who is Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Zirr bin Jaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever spits facing the Qiblah will come on the Day of Resurrection with his spit before his eyes.”"
